7:51Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T16:24:53Z","closed_at":"2026-09-16T16:22:29Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123035","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123035","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123035.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123035.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-16T16:22:29Z"},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n- Supersedes and closes #99769\r\n\r\n    - cc @khairul169\r\n\r\n- Closes #52239 \n- Closes #70975 \r\n\r\nFixes an issue where deleting a file in the Web Editor throws a \"Cannot remove\" error and fails to delete the file.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe delete dialog relies on `OS::move_to_trash()`, but this wasn't implemented for the web platform, causing it to always fail. \r\n\r\nSince the web doesn't have a system trash, this PR implements `OS_Web::move_to_trash()` to permanently delete the files instead (similar to how Android handles it). \r\n\r\nThis uses `DirAccess` for the deletion, which automatically triggers the IndexedDB sync so the file deletions are properly saved to the browser's persistent storage.\r\n\r\n## Before:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/37d45398-857c-4c80-a693-033f5fdb74f7\r\n\r\n## After:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5745c4c3-2f05-46c5-b958-a5550ecfb373\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avata